{"n": 644, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "644.webp", "text": "3411220 REMOVING AND INSTALLING\nFRONT BRAKE DISCS\n\nRemove front wheels 36 10 300.\nUnserew caliper mounting bolts (1)\nInstallation:\n\nTightening torque\",\n\nUnplug brake pad wear indicator on left side.\nPull off caliper toward rear and suspend with a\npiece of wire,\n\nUnscrew bolt (2),\nTake off brake disc\nTool: wrench socket 34 1 020,\n\n* See Specifications\n\ndoa. 025\n\n730 34152\n\n3411599 CHECKING FRONT BRAKE\nDISCS FOR RUNOUT AND\nDEVIATION IN THICKNESS\n\nFrom Wheels Reinowed\n\nRequirement: wheel bearings okay\n\nMount dial gage bolder and check lateral runost\nof brake duc with dial gage\n\nNote:\n\nMount brake dec with two M 12 = 1.5 bolts.\n\nMeasure deviation in thickness® within braking\nsurface at about 8 points with o micrometer\n\n34171667 FINE GRINDING FRONT\nBRAKE DISCS\n— Brake Dises Removed —\n\nimportant!\n\nAlways fine grind both sides of both brake\ndiscs on one axle.\n\nCheck minimum thickness*.\n\nAfter grinding to final size* one more brake\npad set may be installed and worn to limits\n(see wear limit\").\n\ninstalation.\n\nEven if only one brake disc has to be replaced,\nalways replace both brake discs of one axle.\n\n* See Specifications", "words": [["3411220", 0.2604, 0.0628, 0.3099, 0.0734], ["REMOVING", 0.3231, 0.0628, 0.3827, 0.0734], ["AND", 0.3868, 0.0628, 0.41, 0.0734], ["INSTALLING", 0.4156, 0.0628, 0.4823, 0.0734], ["FRONT", 0.3231, 0.0787, 0.3595, 0.0893], ["BRAKE", 0.3645, 0.0787, 0.4009, 0.0893], ["DISCS", 0.406, 0.0787, 0.4368, 0.0893], ["Remove", 0.2604, 0.1124, 0.2998, 0.123], ["front", 0.3028, 0.1124, 0.3271, 0.123], ["wheels", 0.3311, 0.1124, 0.3615, 0.123], ["36", 0.3655, 0.1124, 0.3766, 0.123], ["10", 0.3827, 0.1124, 0.3928, 0.1217], ["300.", 0.3959, 0.1124, 0.4146, 0.1217], ["Unserew", 0.2604, 0.1283, 0.3018, 0.1389], ["caliper", 0.3049, 0.1283, 0.3362, 0.1415], ["mounting", 0.3402, 0.1296, 0.3857, 0.1402], ["bolts", 0.3888, 0.1283, 0.412, 0.1389], [